		)
		(property "Note" "K-line commander pull-up high-side switch. Connects/disconnects R5 (1k) from +12V, replacing the J5 jumper so the mode is software-selectable instead of needing the HAT unstacked from under the dash. GPIO24 high -> Q3 conducts -> R13/R14 divide +12V to 1.09V at this gate -> Vgs = -10.9V, inside the +/-20V limit. GPIO low OR high-Z -> R13 holds the gate at +12V -> Vgs = 0 -> off. So passive sniff mode is the safe default and a Pi that is off, booting or crashed cannot perturb a scan-tool session. Rds(on) ~10 ohm is a 1% error on a 1k pull-up. Body diode conducts D->S, i.e. away from the bus, so with Q2 off the pull-up is genuinely disconnected."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(hide yes)
			(show_name no)
			(do_not_autoplace no)
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
				)
				(justify left)
			)
		)
